<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bab Zuwayla</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bab Zuwayla is the southern gate of Fatimid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cairo">Cairo</a>, built in the late eleventh century under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vizier">vizier</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/badr-al-jamali">Badr al-Jamali</a>. Its twin towers later had minarets added on top. It is one of the three surviving Fatimid city gates and a landmark of medieval Cairo.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bab-zuwayla.jpg" alt="Bab Zuwayla" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: JMCC1 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bab_Zuwayla_Cairo_12_0864.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
